---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation system"
  path="/docs/maintainers/documentation"
  description="Canonical Markdown, generated MDX mirrors, the validation contract, and how this site is built and deployed."
>
  <p>
    KoAkademy's documentation has a single-source rule: <strong
      >root Markdown files are canonical</strong
    > for project and technical docs; the Astro site and the in-app docs viewer consume
    <strong>generated mirrors</strong>. This page is the maintainer's map of
    that machinery.
  </p>

  <h2>The pipeline</h2>
  <pre><code>Root canonical MD ──▶ scripts/sync-docs.mjs ──▶ MDX mirrors (site + in-app viewer)
        │                                              ▲
        └────── scripts/check-docs.mjs (validation) ◀──┘</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>npm run docs:sync</code> maps eight canonical files to site pages:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Canonical source</th>
        <th>Generated page</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>GETTING_STARTED.md</code></td>
        <td>Self-Hosting → Installation</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>DEPLOYMENT.md</code></td>
        <td>Self-Hosting → Deployment</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>CONFIGURATION.md</code></td>
        <td>Self-Hosting → Configuration</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>TROUBLESHOOTING.md</code></td>
        <td>Self-Hosting → Troubleshooting</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>FAQ.md</code></td>
        <td>Self-Hosting → FAQ</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>DEVELOPMENT.md</code></td>
        <td>Start Here → Development</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ARCHITECTURE.md</code></td>
        <td>Start Here → Architecture</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code></td>
        <td>Start Here → Contributing</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The generator strips the source H1, prepends Starlight frontmatter and a
    <code>&#123;/* GENERATED FILE… */&#125;</code> warning, and rewrites cross-doc
    links: mirrored docs become site routes; repo-only docs (<code
      >README.md</code
    >,
    <code>SECURITY.md</code>, <code>CHANGELOG.md</code>,
    <code>LICENSE.md</code>) become absolute GitHub URLs. <strong
      >Never edit a generated mirror</strong
    > — edit the canonical file and re-run the sync. Target directories are created
    automatically.
  </p>
  <p>
    Everything else on the site — System Internals, Maintainers, the User Guide,
    Enrollment Blueprints, API docs — is <strong>native MDX</strong>, edited in
    place under <code>docs/src/content/docs/</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Validation (<code>npm run docs:check</code>)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <code>sync-docs.mjs --check</code> — fails if any generated mirror is stale.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>scripts/check-docs.mjs</code> — verifies all canonical files exist, every
      local <code>.md</code>/<code>.mdx</code> link across root docs and site content
      resolves, the three tested API endpoints (<code
        >GET /api/v1/public/settings</code
      >, <code>GET /api/settings</code>,
      <code>POST /api/students/verify</code>) are documented, and fictional
      student-CRUD endpoints were not reintroduced.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    CI runs both on every push and PR (see
    <a href="/docs/maintainers/ci">CI pipeline</a>); run them before committing
    doc changes.
  </p>

  <h2>The site itself</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stack:</strong> Astro 5 + Starlight, MDX content collection, Pagefind
      search, sitemap — built with Node 22 (<code
        >npm --prefix docs ci &amp;&amp; npm --prefix docs run build</code
      >).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme:</strong>
      <code>docs/src/styles/custom.css</code> maps the app's shadcn palette onto Starlight
      with self-hosted Inter/JetBrains Mono (fontsource — no external requests).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Navigation:</strong> the explicit sidebar in
      <code>docs/astro.config.mjs</code>. New pages need a sidebar entry or they
      exist but are unreachable.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In-app viewer:</strong> the same generated mirrors render inside the
      application at <code>/docs</code>, so operator docs ship with the product.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deployment</h2>
  <p>
    <code>deploy-docs.yml</code> builds the site and can deploy it through
    <code>upload-pages-artifact</code> + <code>deploy-pages</code>. The workflow
    is intentionally disabled while the repository is private.
  </p>
  <p>After the repository becomes public:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Enable <strong
        >Settings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source: GitHub Actions</strong
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      Run <code
        >gh workflow enable deploy-docs.yml --repo yukazakiri/koakademy</code
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      Push a change under <code>docs/**</code> or manually dispatch the workflow.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Successful deployments publish at
    <code>https://yukazakiri.github.io/koakademy/</code> (the
    <code>site</code>/<code>base</code> in <code>astro.config.mjs</code> — keep them
    in sync if the repository ever moves).
  </p>

  <h2>Writing guidelines for maintainers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Factual over aspirational.</strong> Document what the code does today;
      roadmaps live in issues/projects, not docs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Screenshots</strong> go in <code>docs/src/assets/</code> and are imported
      by MDX (optimized at build).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>API surface:</strong> only tested endpoints may be documented — the
      contract check enforces it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Security and changelog</strong> stay on GitHub (SECURITY.md, Releases)
      and are deliberately not mirrored to the site.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
